{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent negative bias: forecasts are systematically too low versus realized prices, especially in rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift (≈ +2 to +5 €/t on average), increasing with forecast horizon.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the last 1–2 weeks show an upswing, the model fails to propagate momentum. Add a trend-following adjustment proportional to recent slope (e.g., add ~0.2–0.4× the 10–15d linear trend to the whole path).",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: error grows with lead time (largest in weeks 2–4). Use a ramped correction: small uplift in days 1–5, larger uplift in days 10–30.",
    "Insufficient amplitude after regime shift: after a breakout from low-60s to high-60s, the model keeps reverting toward mid-60s. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making higher highs/higher lows over the last ~10 days.",
    "Post-spike behavior: model often predicts mild pullbacks/sideways while realized continues higher. After a strong up-day cluster, dampen any forecasted retracement and bias the next 5–15 days upward unless recent volatility is collapsing."
  ]
}
